# K03d, migrated by K03-EXPLICIT-RECEIVER-FRAMES: this row pinned `w: merge Model`, the atom spelling
# the author (2026-10-06) calls a typo; it is the Frame `w: merge: Model`.  The destination is not a
# first operand, and not a new declaration when the name is already bound -- `w` is an int here, so the
# statement assigns a merge value to an existing binding, which the current receiving-context machinery
# refuses.  The message is the assignment path's current one, not a claim of the language.
# The atom spelling's reading is gone with the other atom readings.
Model: (int: value 1)
fn: m () int
    int: w 5
    w: merge: Model
    return: w\value
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
